# Candidate implementation — Task 0003

**Task:** [0003 — Integer Calculator](../../../examples/0003-calculator.md)  
**Status:** Illustrative LLMLang semantic sketch; not parsed, built, executed, or formally verified.

The sketch uses abstract standard-library operations such as `parse_i64`, `checked_add`, and `checked_div`. Their exact LLMLang signatures and semantics must be specified before this can become executable source.

```text
type CalcError =
    InvalidInput
    DivisionByZero
    ArithmeticOverflow

type Expression:
    left: Int64
    operator: Char
    right: Int64

operation parse_expression(line: String) -> Result<Expression, CalcError>:
    tokens = split_ascii_whitespace(line)

    if tokens.length != 3:
        return Error(InvalidInput)

    left = parse_i64(tokens[0])
    right = parse_i64(tokens[2])

    if left is Error or right is Error:
        return Error(InvalidInput)

    if tokens[1].length != 1:
        return Error(InvalidInput)

    operator = tokens[1][0]
    if operator not in ['+', '-', '*', '/']:
        return Error(InvalidInput)

    return Ok(Expression(left.value, operator, right.value))

operation evaluate(expression: Expression) -> Result<Int64, CalcError>:
    match expression.operator:
        '+':
            return checked_add(expression.left, expression.right)
                .map_error(ArithmeticOverflow)
        '-':
            return checked_sub(expression.left, expression.right)
                .map_error(ArithmeticOverflow)
        '*':
            return checked_mul(expression.left, expression.right)
                .map_error(ArithmeticOverflow)
        '/':
            if expression.right == 0:
                return Error(DivisionByZero)
            return checked_div_trunc_zero(expression.left, expression.right)
                .map_error(ArithmeticOverflow)
        _:
            return Error(InvalidInput)

main:
    line = stdin.read_line_or_eof()
    if line is Error:
        report InvalidInput
    if line is Eof:
        report InvalidInput

    expression = parse_expression(line)
    if expression is Error:
        report expression.error

    result = evaluate(expression.value)
    if result is Error:
        report result.error

    match stdout.write_utf8(format_i64(result.value) + "\n"):
        Ok:
            exit(0)
        Error(_):
            exit(1)

report(error: CalcError):
    stderr.write_utf8(match error:
        InvalidInput       => "invalid input\n"
        DivisionByZero     => "division by zero\n"
        ArithmeticOverflow => "arithmetic overflow\n"
    )
    exit(1)
```

## Requirement mapping

| Requirement | Implementation |
|---|---|
| R-0003-01 | `parse_expression` requires exactly three tokens |
| R-0003-02 | `parse_i64` enforces signed 64-bit range |
| R-0003-03 | Operator whitelist |
| R-0003-04 | Checked addition, subtraction, multiplication |
| R-0003-05 | `checked_div_trunc_zero` |
| R-0003-06 | Explicit zero-divisor branch |
| R-0003-07 | Checked arithmetic maps overflow, including MIN / -1 |
| R-0003-08 | Canonical integer formatting, LF, exit 0 |
| R-0003-09 | Error-specific stderr line, no stdout result, nonzero exit |
| R-0003-10 | ASCII-whitespace tokenization and exact token count |

